% review-findings: No words under the notes; the title names Nirguna, the supreme being in Hindu thought, and the book's prose translation is a tired mother's lullaby (celestial carpenters made the cradle; my baby is not yet asleep).
% review-suggestion: Keep; label it a devotional lullaby. Nothing in the words to change.
